.TH env_merge 3
.SH NAME
env_merge \- merge environment modifications into an array
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>

.B size_t env_merge(const char** \fIv\fP, size_t \fIvmax\fP, const char* const* \fIenvp\fP, size_t \fIenvlen\fP, const char* \fImodifs\fP, size_t \fImodiflen\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env_merge
merges modifications (\fImodifs\fP) into an existing environment array \fIenvp\fP, 
storing the results in \fIv\fP. Modifications are expected as a null-terminated 
concatenation of strings. Variables in \fImodifs\fP replace existing variables 
in \fIenvp\fP.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The new number of elements in the merged array, or 0 if \fIvmax\fP is exceeded.